From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:48:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/perf: apple_m1: Fix a typo in a comment

"mimick" should be "mimic", and the sentence lacked its full stop.

Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c b/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c
index edac4b20cd4d..a67a364a931c 100644
--- a/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/perf/apple_m1_cpu_pmu.c
@@ -967,7 +967,7 @@ static int apple_pmu_map_event(struct perf_event *event,
  * 64 bits wide, depending on the SoC. However, the MSB is
  * what triggers an overflow interrupt, so we advertise the
  * counters as being 1-bit smaller than hardware allows to
- * mimick ARM PMU behaviour
+ * mimic ARM PMU behaviour.
  */
 static int m1_pmu_map_event(struct perf_event *event)
 {
